values ('a8b9c0d1-3e4f-4a58-9b78-8c9d0e1f2a88', 'research-methods-in-social-work', 'Research Methods in Social Work', 'Students learn why social work research exists: to improve services, test assumptions, honor client knowledge, and make practice accountable to evidence and justice. They turn practice problems into researchable questions grounded in scholarship, theory, and lived experience; study ethics, IRB review, anti-oppressive research, and community accountability; match designs to claims about needs, experiences, programs, outcomes, and causal change; and cover sampling, culturally responsive measurement, surveys, quantitative and qualitative analysis, mixed and community-engaged inquiry, evidence appraisal, practice and program evaluation, research communication, and an applied research or evaluation proposal.');

